  "title": "German Revolution of 1918–1919",
  "summary": "Revolution at the end of the First World War. A naval mutiny set off workers' and soldiers' councils across Germany, and on 9 November 1918 the Kaiser's abdication was declared in Berlin and a republic proclaimed. Social Democrat Friedrich Ebert took over, and the Weimar Constitution took effect on 11 August 1919.",
